language ESSENCE' 1.0
$ Mario starts at his house, collects gold on a route and returns to his house via Luigi's house. Houses are numbered 0 to nHouses-1. s[i] is the house after house i-1 on the route (1-based index i), and s[i] = i-1 when house i-1 is not on the route.
given nHouses : int(2..15)
given marioHouse : int(0..nHouses-1)
given luigiHouse : int(0..nHouses-1)
given fuelLimit : int(0..)
given arc_fuel : matrix indexed by [int(1..nHouses), int(1..nHouses)] of int(0..)
given goldInHouse : matrix indexed by [int(1..nHouses)] of int(0..)
find s : matrix indexed by [int(1..nHouses)] of int(0..nHouses-1)
find pos : matrix indexed by [int(1..nHouses)] of int(0..nHouses-1)

maximising (sum i : int(1..nHouses) . toInt(s[i] != i - 1) * goldInHouse[i])

such that
$ the successor function is a permutation of the houses
allDiff(s),
$ Mario's house is on the route, so he leaves it
s[marioHouse+1] != marioHouse,
$ Luigi's house is followed by Mario's house, which closes the route
s[luigiHouse+1] = marioHouse,
$ the route starts at Mario's house at position 0
pos[marioHouse+1] = 0,
$ along the route each house is one step after the house before it, so no separate cycle avoids Mario's house
forAll i : int(1..nHouses) . ((s[i] != i - 1 /\ s[i] != marioHouse) -> pos[s[i]+1] = pos[i] + 1),
$ the total fuel of the arcs taken must not exceed the fuel limit
(sum i : int(1..nHouses) . arc_fuel[i, s[i]+1]) <= fuelLimit
